# Application Architecture

## Routing & Pages
The application uses Next.js App Router architecture with the following structure:
- [src/app/page.tsx](mdc:src/app/page.tsx): Main landing page
- [src/app/(dashboard)](mdc:src/app/(dashboard)): Dashboard routes (authenticated)
- [src/app/(auth)](mdc:src/app/(auth)): Authentication routes
- [src/app/layout.tsx](mdc:src/app/layout.tsx): Root layout with providers

## Components Organization
- [src/components/ui](mdc:src/components/ui): Reusable UI components (buttons, inputs, etc.)
- [src/components/editor](mdc:src/components/editor): Presentation editor components
- [src/components/viewer](mdc:src/components/viewer): Presentation viewer components
- [src/components/tiptap](mdc:src/components/tiptap): Rich text editor customizations

## State Management
The application uses Zustand for state management:
- Editor state (current slide, selected elements)
- User preferences
- Application settings

## Authentication
NextAuth.js is used for authentication with MongoDB as the database.